WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.601
-Guys, we have exactly
12 shows left

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.601
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time for

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:06.000
that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.868
It's time for "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters."

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:10.167
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.567
-♪ 12 days of
Christmas sweaters ♪

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:16.734
♪ 12 days left ♪

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:17.834
-That's right.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.467
Every show between
now and Christmas,

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:21.634
we'll be giving one lucky
audience member

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:24.033
an out-of-this-world
Christmas sweater

00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:26.467
from the "Countdown to
Christmas" cabinet.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:32.167
Now, since there are 12 shows
left, let's open door number 12.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:36.367
[ Drumroll ]

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.501
Whoa!

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:41.033
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:42.501
Let's see it.

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:44.701
Wow. Look at that.
Oh, my goodness.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:47.467
That is unbelievable.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:48.901
Wow!

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:51.133
Can we -- Is there a back to it?
Yeah.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:52.734
Oh, wow!

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:54.734
Oh!

00:00:54.734 --> 00:00:57.100
It's got, like --
It's got, like,

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.000
almost like
a Pop-Tart back to it.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.667
It looks like a Pop-Tart.
I like it.

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.067
Very, very nice.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:04.133
Let's see who is going to go
home with tonight's sweater.

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:06.934
Everyone, look at your
seat number, please.

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:08.100
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.901
And, Quest,
can I get a drumroll, please?

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:13.367
[ Drumroll ]

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:18.200
295!

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.167
Yeah!

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:25.901
Yeah!

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:28.367
-Whoo!

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:30.467
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:32.534
Oh, I'm so happy!

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:35.400
You go over there.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.767
Hello!

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:39.734
I'm so excited that you won.

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:41.467
What is your name?
And where are you from?

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.868
-My name is Nadeesha,
and I'm from Midtown East.

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:49.033
-Welcome. Thank you so much
for being here.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:50.634
Well, where did you say
you were from, again?

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:52.133
-Well, I live in
Midtown East now.

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:53.501
-Midtown.
-Midtown, yes.

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:56.400
-Oh, yeah, but east of Midtown.
-Yes, the better side.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.501
-Be more specific.

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:58.501
It's like,
"What's your actual address

00:01:58.501 --> 00:01:59.501
so we can all send you things."

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:01.100
No, don't do that.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.968
But here in Midtown,
it does get a little chilly.

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.434
-Yes, it does.
-And we're getting ready.

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:06.267
Do you have a
sweater or anything like this?

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:08.667
-No, I don't.
-Wow!

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.467
Would you like to try it on now?
-Yeah.

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:12.067
-We'd all love to see it.
Wouldn't you love to see it?

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.601
Here's this...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:15.601
♪♪

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.133
Are you kidding me?

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:23.634
You are a knockout.

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.267
Look at this.
Are you joking?

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:27.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, walk the runway.

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:29.601
You got it. Oh!

00:02:29.601 --> 00:02:31.601
[ Laughs ]

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.968
You are a star.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:37.601
Give it up for our winner.
A round of applause.

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:38.734
Stick around.

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.834
We're playing
"Off Songs, Song Off"

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:42.200
with Blake Shelton
after the break.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.767
You look gorgeous.
I love it.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:44.868
That's a rad sweater.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:46.801
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

